From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:42:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Retro belongs in Demos, because that is what it is

Retro exists to show what a game pane does -- an indexed world the host's GPU
turns into pixels, sprites, per-scanline palettes, a shader you can replace at
run time. It is a demonstration, not a game, and it sat in the Games folder
next to Minesweeper because /boot/system/apps is where applications go.

SYSTEM_DEMOS installs to /boot/system/demos, which is what the Deskbar's Demos
folder links to, so that is where it goes. Galaxigans stays in Games: it is one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0121-retro-belongs-in-demos-because-that-is-what-it-is.patch 59c8996ac01e952d56756e2bc3906ace53bee3b7b6957892fce87f5d1b41596d
